From: A50 port <noreply@example.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fimc-is: close the open() race that panics the kernel

Opening an SSx V4L2 node concurrently panics this SoC, reproducibly:

  8 simultaneous opens of /dev/video101 (exynos-fimc-is-ss0)
  -> uptime 1211s -> 15s, every time

with the bootloader's crash record naming it exactly:

  "PC":"fimc_is_devicemgr_open+0x1e8/0x3a0"
  "STACK":"fimc_is_devicemgr_open:fimc_is_sensor_open:
           fimc_is_ssx_video_open:v4l2_open:chrdev_open:vfs_open:
           path_openat:do_filp_open:SyS_openat"
  "RR":"KP"   "KTIME":"1211"

The faulting instruction, from the built vmlinux, is

  +0x1e4:  ldr x8, [x19, #272]     ; x8 = sensor->vctx
  +0x1e8:  str x22, [x8, #9136]    ; sensor->vctx->next_device = ischain

so vctx is non-NULL, passes FIMC_BUG(!sensor->vctx) at +0x40, and still
faults: it is dangling, not null.

The cause is a plain test-then-set with a 91 line window:

  1712   if (test_bit(FIMC_IS_SENSOR_OPEN, &device->state))  <- check
  1739       device->vctx = vctx;
  1787       fimc_is_devicemgr_open(...)                      <- faults
  1803   set_bit(FIMC_IS_SENSOR_OPEN, &device->state);        <- set

Nothing serialises fimc_is_sensor_open(). Two opens both pass the check
before either sets the bit, both write the shared device->vctx, and when
one unwinds through its error path and frees its video context the other
dereferences it.

test_and_set_bit() closes the window atomically. The error paths inside it
must then release the bit, so err_open_state clears it; the already-open
case gets its own label, because there the bit belongs to the other opener
and must not be touched. The later set_bit at 1803 becomes redundant and
is left alone.

This is Samsung vendor code; fimc-is2 is not in mainline (mainline carries
exynos4-is), so there is no upstream to send this to.

--- a/drivers/media/platform/exynos/fimc-is2/fimc-is-device-sensor_v2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/exynos/fimc-is2/fimc-is-device-sensor_v2.c
@@ -1709,9 +1709,9 @@
 
 	core = device->private_data;
 
-	if (test_bit(FIMC_IS_SENSOR_OPEN, &device->state)) {
+	if (test_and_set_bit(FIMC_IS_SENSOR_OPEN, &device->state)) {
 		merr("already open", device);
 		ret = -EMFILE;
-		goto err_open_state;
+		goto err_already_open;
 	}
 
@@ -1822,7 +1822,9 @@
 	if (ret_err)
 		merr("fimc_is_csi_close is fail(%d)", device, ret_err);
 err_csi_open:
 err_camif_open:
 err_open_state:
+	clear_bit(FIMC_IS_SENSOR_OPEN, &device->state);
+err_already_open:
 	minfo("[SEN:D] %s():%d\n", device, __func__, ret);
 	return ret;
